1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
What’s new in Island Time 1.23.0, shown with mock game data.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,000
The title screen now has a card for each way to play: Islander and Visitor.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,500
Each card has its own Continue, Start a new game and Saves.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,000
Each way to play keeps up to three games, six in all.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,500
Your saved games were moved onto the right card when you updated. Nothing was lost.

6
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:27,000
Visits and weekend regular games live on the Visitor side.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,500
A weekend regular who buys the house moves to an Islander slot on their own.

8
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:36,000
Visitors get their own levels: Easy Sunday, Tourist and Missed the Boat.

9
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,500
They change your budget, I-5 traffic, crashes, the boats and the last-boat warning.

10
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:45,000
The top of the screen always shows which way you’re playing, and at what level.

11
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,500
Islanders keep Normal and Ferry Hell. The easy level is now called Old-timer.

12
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:55,000
Play free in your browser at krazow.github.io/islandtime

